  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Coupling a metabolite input to the gate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive \u2014 Replace one synthetic input with a real metabolite sensor, and measure what that costs."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Design"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The arabinose-responsive "
          },
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-77b7ffc5",
              "label": "C0080 (AraC)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-77b7ffc5",
              "path": "sequences/kits/moclo-cidar/C0080_CD",
              "contentHash": null,
              "objectUuid": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and its promoter replace the third synthetic input. LuxR is retained on the second input, which is why the entry-13 swap was deferred."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Why this is the honest test"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A gate driven by three orthogonal synthetic inducers is a demonstration. A gate driven by a metabolite the host also metabolises is the actual application, and it is strictly harder: the input concentration changes during the experiment because the cells consume it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ON/OFF falls to 11-fold, below criterion. The loss is not crosstalk \u2014 it is input depletion: arabinose is consumed within 90 minutes, so the ON state decays during the measurement window."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Consequence"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A non-metabolisable analogue, or an arabinose-catabolism-deficient host, is required. Recorded as the primary open problem in entry 18."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
